{"name":"Trinidad Moruga Scorpion","hex":"#d0343d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scorpion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the order Scorpiones of arachnids related to spiders, characterised by two large front pincers and a curved tail with a venomous sting at the end.","An ancient military engine for hurling stones and other missiles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scorpion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trinidad Moruga scorpion","blocks":[{"text":"The Trinidad Moruga scorpion is a chili pepper native to the village of Moruga, Trinidad and Tobago. In 2012, New Mexico State University's Chile Pepper Institute identified the Trinidad Moruga scorpion as the hottest chili pepper at that time, with heat of 1.2 million Scoville heat units (SHUs)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Trinidad_Moruga_Scorpion.jpg/330px-Trinidad_Moruga_Scorpion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidad_Moruga_scorpion"},{"title":"Trinidad","blocks":[{"text":"Trinidad is the largest and most populous island of the Republic of Trinidad and Tobago. The island lies 11 km (7 mi) off the northeastern coast of Venezuela and sits on the continental shelf of South America. It is the southernmost island in the Caribbean. With an area of 4,768 km2 (1,841 sq mi), it is also the fifth-largest in the Caribbean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Td-map.png/330px-Td-map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidad"},{"title":"Moruga","blocks":[{"text":"The village of Moruga lies on the central south coast of Trinidad at the western end of the Trinity Hills. It is in Princes Town region and is served by the Princes Town Regional Corporation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Moruga_-_Village_on_the_south_coast_of_Trinidad%2C_West_Indies.jpg/330px-Moruga_-_Village_on_the_south_coast_of_Trinidad%2C_West_Indies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moruga"},{"title":"Scorpion","blocks":[{"text":"Scorpions are predatory arachnids with eight legs, a pair of grasping pincers and a narrow, segmented tail, often carried in a characteristic forward curve over the back and always ending with a stinger. The evolutionary history of scorpions goes back to the Silurian Period, approximately 430 million years ago. They mainly live in deserts but have adapted to a wide range of environmental conditions, and can be found on all continents except Antarctica. There are over 2,500 described species, with 22 extant (living) families recognized to date. Their taxonomy is being revised to account for 21st-century genomic studies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Scorpion_Photograph_By_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg/330px-Scorpion_Photograph_By_Shantanu_Kuveskar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scorpion"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Trinidad_moruga_scorpion_ripe_ready_to_pick.jpg/500px-Trinidad_moruga_scorpion_ripe_ready_to_pick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Trinidad_moruga_scorpion_ripe_ready_to_pick.jpg/500px-Trinidad_moruga_scorpion_ripe_ready_to_pick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Trinidad Moruga scorpion, ripe and ready to pick","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrinidad_moruga_scorpion_ripe_ready_to_pick.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Moruga_-_Christopher_Columbus_monument.jpg/500px-Moruga_-_Christopher_Columbus_monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wik